index 0000000..f30d489
--- /dev/null
+++ b/context/testing/verifiability-matrix.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Verifiability matrix — winter-test-service
+
+The methods by which changes to this application are verified against runtime
+behavior. Each row carries a stable `<scope>:<method>` id so the same check can
+be selected and rerun by the next change and the next agent, rather than being
+re-improvised.
+
+This repository has **no automated unit/integration test suite**; verification
+is performed against a **running stack** (`winter service up <env> --wait`, or a
+plain local run per `README.md`). The rows below are the durable, rerunnable
+mechanisms for that.
+
+## Commands
+
+| Method id | Verifies | Command |
+|-----------|----------|---------|
+| `api:item-lifecycle` | The item HTTP API end-to-end: `GET /api/health`, `POST /api/items` (create, 201, `source=api`), `DELETE /api/items/{id}` (204 + empty body on success, 404 on a missing/already-deleted id), and that a delete removes exactly the targeted row while other rows survive. | `scripts/verify_item_api.sh [BASE_URL]` — `BASE_URL` defaults to `$WTS_API_BASE_URL` then the api's default local port (see README → Configuration); in a winter env pass the env's api base URL (e.g. `scripts/verify_item_api.sh http://localhost:6031`). Exit 0 iff all checks pass. Requires `bash`, `curl`, `jq`. |
+
+### Notes
+
+- `api:item-lifecycle` covers the delete endpoint (`DELETE /api/items/{item_id}`)
+  and doubles as a regression check for health, create, and list. It self-provisions
+  its own fixtures (creates a keeper + a delete target), so it needs no seed step.
+- The "removed exactly one row" assertion diffs the `GET /api/items` id set before
+  and after the delete. That endpoint returns at most 100 rows newest-first, so the
+  diff is exact only while the table is under that window; the script notes this in a
+  comment. The worker inserts a heartbeat row every couple of seconds, so ids grow
+  during a run — the check accounts for insert-only churn.
+- The api and worker processes run with no auto-reload (`uv run python -m app` /
+  `python -m worker.main`, no `--reload`) — unlike the web dev server, which does
+  hot-reload. After editing api/worker Python, restart the process (`./restart api`
+  / `./restart worker` from the feature-env directory) before rerunning this check,
+  or it will silently exercise the pre-edit code.
+
+## Manual testing
+
+| Method id | Verifies | Exercise |
+|-----------|----------|----------|
+| `web:item-delete` | The web UI's per-row delete control: clicking it removes the row without a full page reload, the deletion persists server-side, and add/list/health still work. | Browser exercise against the running web UI (e.g. http://localhost:`$WTS_WEB_PORT`) — requires a browser-capable verifier; out of scope for a `Bash`-only agent. Add an item, click its Delete button, confirm the row disappears with no page reload, and confirm via `GET /api/items` that it's gone server-side. |
+
+## Tools
+
+_(none yet — `api:item-lifecycle` is self-provisioning; add seed/reset tooling here if a future check needs pre-existing state it cannot create for itself.)_
